WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.269 --> 00:00:06.220
Some bread, a warm meal, - or even socks:
Migrants are getting help from individuals

00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:10.449
and institutions, like in this hostel in Mexico
City.

00:00:10.449 --> 00:00:13.279
Viviana Gutierrez is one of those who turned
out.

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:20.190
Today she drove a van over loaded with clothes
for women and children.

00:00:20.190 --> 00:00:23.550
It's gratifying that a lot of people are helping.

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:30.170
It brings out the humanity in us and it pleases
me to see the difference we are making.

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:34.970
We're all very proud to be Mexican.

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:39.660
Mexico has seen migrants bound northwards
travel through the country for decades.

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:45.550
This is a chance for it to express solidarity
with foreigners.

00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:50.150
We have to deal with this acutely painful
situation, to reach out to people passing

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:54.730
through who are in need."

00:00:54.730 --> 00:00:59.079
Colombians and Hondurans think that we reject
them, but we have to support each other because

00:00:59.079 --> 00:01:05.110
we are all human beings, and we feel for them."

00:01:05.110 --> 00:01:09.789
But these people haven't been welcomed by
everyone...

00:01:09.789 --> 00:01:14.170
Some Mexicans have begun lashing out at the
migrants.

00:01:14.170 --> 00:01:17.929
"They have no problems because they don't
work.

00:01:17.929 --> 00:01:19.439
If they come here to contribute, they're welcome.

00:01:19.439 --> 00:01:24.340
It seems like they're having a day at the
beach - they don't wear shirts, they throw

00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:29.670
away the food we give them, but they keep
the beer."

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:33.450
Many of them are drunk, urinating in public
everywhere.

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:35.509
Mexico cannot cope with receiving them.

00:01:35.509 --> 00:01:40.530
I hope that from now on officials check their
papers and give them what they deserve, and

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:42.590
give us what we deserve.

00:01:42.590 --> 00:01:49.399
Their human rights are apparently worth more
than ours.

00:01:49.399 --> 00:01:54.899
Some of the migrants have felt that lack of
sensitivity during their journey.

00:01:54.899 --> 00:02:01.039
But even so, most say Mexico has offered them
good care.

00:02:01.039 --> 00:02:04.509
Just now one person insulted us.

00:02:04.509 --> 00:02:07.560
We didn't like that but I guess we have to
accept it.

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:12.030
We are invading their country"

00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:16.220
"Mexico has received us very well.

00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:22.320
We are very proud because it has given us
all this support, we have not lacked food,

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:25.170
clothing."

00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:29.250
Mexico - a country divided, like so many others,
by migration.

